# Rendered assets and source rasters live outside git (see CLAUDE.md)
data/
*.part
blender/renders/
blender/*.png
*.blend1
# Hero .blend scenes are build artifacts — regenerate with pipeline/scene_build.py
# (thin ~96K files that reference gitignored rasters, so a committed copy can't
# even open on a fresh clone). The source of truth is scene_build.py. The one
# exception is the hand-built Phase 0 scene, which no script reproduces.
blender/*.blend
!blender/india_hero_handbuilt_phase0.blend

# CLAUDE.md is TRACKED, deliberately: it is the standing brief for anyone — human or agent —
# working on this repo, and shipping it is the honest version of "here is how this was built".
# It states current truth only; the dated record stays in the archive below.

# Working documents, deliberately untracked: the dated decision archive and the standing brief for
# the second body are how the work gets done, not what it ships. Nothing tracked cites them — a
# shipped file must never point at something a clone does not have — so the repo reads complete
# without them, and `test_no_reference_to_a_file_a_clone_will_not_have` is what keeps that true.
#
# UNTRACKING A FILE THAT OTHER BRANCHES STILL TRACK IS THE DANGEROUS HALF, not the ignore line.
# Checking out any branch where the path is tracked makes git materialise its version over the
# working copy, and because the path is ignored here it does so SILENTLY, exit 0. That is how six
# HISTORY entries were destroyed. The files that still exist are snapshotted outside the repo and
# restored by `guard-working-docs.py`, which also records why PLAN.md is deliberately not among them.
PLAN.md
HISTORY.md
MARS.md
# Guards the archive's index and anchors, so it travels with its subject: in a clone without the
# archive it could only fail, and it keeps running locally where the file does exist.
tests/test_history_integrity.py

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Phase 2 geotools binaries — vendored, reinstall with pipeline/install_geotools.sh
tools/

# Secrets — never commit (holds OPENTOPOGRAPHY_API_KEY; OT prohibits sharing keys)
.env
.env.*

# Local prod-sim TLS cert (deploy/make-local-cert.sh regenerates it)
deploy/certs/

# Coverage data (uv run pytest --cov)
.coverage

# wrangler's local state — deploy/build cache and dev-server storage, regenerated on
# demand. Written wherever a wrangler command is run, so this is deliberately unanchored.
.wrangler/

# Per-author agent instructions, loaded from disk when a matching file is opened. They are one
# person's working notes rather than a project standard, so committing them would put a second,
# unowned set of instructions beside CLAUDE.md. Everything a contributor must follow belongs in
# CLAUDE.md, which IS tracked. Same posture as .claude/settings.local.json.
.claude/rules/
